me":"knowledge_notes/kernel知识笔记/Flexible Token Dispatcher (CUDA Kernel).md","basename":"Flexible Token Dispatcher (CUDA Kernel)","score":117.27480916413978,"foundWords":["warps","schedule","gpu","gpu，同时平衡各","gpus,","gpus","gpu。但"],"matches":[{"match":"GPU。但","offset":267},{"match":"GPU","offset":321},{"match":"GPU，同时平衡各","offset":383},{"match":"GPU","offset":393},{"match":"schedule","offset":453},{"match":"schedule","offset":712},{"match":"GPUs,","offset":1004},{"match":"schedule","offset":1331},{"match":"schedule","offset":2902},{"match":"warps","offset":2987}],"excerpt":"…ment 下的高效 token dispatch。在传统 EP 中，每 expert 仅有一个 replica，token dispatch 是简单的：将 token 发送到持有该 expert 的 GPU。但 Lazarus 为 popular experts 分配了不同数量的 replicas 在不同 GPU 上（非对称 placement），需要决定每个 token 具体发往哪个持有目标 expert replica 的 GPU，同时平衡各 GPU 负载。\n该 kernel 对所有 E 个 experts 和 N 个 ranks 并行计算 dispatch schedule。核心逻辑：(a) 计算每个 expert 的每 replica 应处理的 token 数 p_e = t_e / r_e（负载均衡）；(b) 计算每个 rank 对每个 expert 的处理容量 P_{e,j}…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/kernel知识笔记/Thread Block Specialization (for Fused Communication-Computation Kernels).md","basename":"Thread Block Specialization (for Fused Communication-Computation Kernels)","score":113.36387250146174,"foundWords":["warp","warp:","scheduler","gpu"],"matches":[{"match":"GPU","offset":172},{"match":"GPU","offset":210},{"match":"scheduler","offset":223},{"match":"warp","offset":494},{"match":"warp","offset":575},{"match":"GPU","offset":686},{"match":"warp:","offset":1114},{"match":"warp:","offset":1306}],"excerpt":"Thread Block Specialization 是 Comet 提出的 fused kernel 设计模式，将通信（NVSHMEM I/O）和计算（GEMM）分配到同一 GPU kernel 内但隔离到不同的 thread blocks 中，由 GPU hardware scheduler 并发调度。这替代了传统的\"垂直融合\"（在 GEMM thread block 的 prologue/epilogue 中插入通信 I/O），避免了 fine-grained I/O 干扰高性能计算流水线（尤其在 Hopper TMA 异步流水线中）。\n术语是什么？\n在 Comet 的 fused kernel 中，两类 thread block 共存于同一 kernel launch：\n- **GEMM Thread Blocks**（n^p 个）：使用标准 CUTLAS…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/硬件知识笔记/Limiting Resource (SM Thread Block Scheduling).md","basename":"Limiting Resource (SM Thread Block Scheduling)","score":108.64935678265792,"foundWords":["warps/sm","warps","scheduler","gpu","gpus"],"matches":[{"match":"GPU","offset":84},{"match":"scheduler","offset":167},{"match":"warps/SM","offset":256},{"match":"warps","offset":752},{"match":"warps","offset":771},{"match":"scheduler","offset":850},{"match":"GPU","offset":1992},{"match":"warps/SM","offset":2071},{"match":"warps/SM","offset":2130},{"match":"warps/SM","offset":2197},{"match":"scheduler","offset":2240},{"match":"GPU","offset":2519},{"match":"GPU","offset":2640},{"match":"GPU","offset":2806},{"match":"Scheduler","offset":2823},{"match":"GPUs","offset":2907}],"excerpt":"Limiting Resource 是在 NVIDIA GPU most-room policy 下，决定一个 SM 最多能容纳多少新 kernel thread block 的瓶颈资源维度。当 thread block scheduler 计算各 SM 能容纳的 block 数量时，取所有 SM 资源维度（threads、shared memory、registers、blocks/SM 上限、warps/SM 上限）的最小容纳值作为该 SM 的可用容量。Limiting resource 的变化（如 thread/block 从 33→32）可能完全改变 block 的 placement，导致性能的巨大差异。\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/硬件知识笔记/SM Occupancy.md","basename":"SM Occupancy","score":96.94522433639094,"foundWords":["warp","scheduler","gpu","gpus"],"matches":[{"match":"GPU","offset":50},{"match":"warp","offset":93},{"match":"warp","offset":112},{"match":"GPU","offset":140},{"match":"GPU","offset":163},{"match":"warp","offset":241},{"match":"GPU","offset":333},{"match":"GPU","offset":356},{"match":"GPU","offset":501},{"match":"GPU","offset":529},{"match":"GPU","offset":589},{"match":"warp","offset":661},{"match":"warp","offset":686},{"match":"Warp","offset":760},{"match":"scheduler","offset":765},{"match":"warp","offset":782},{"match":"warp","offset":816},{"match":"warp","offset":836},{"match":"GPU","offset":884},{"match":"GPU","offset":951},{"match":"GPU","offset":1174},{"match":"GPU","offset":1466},{"match":"GPUs","offset":1655}],"excerpt":"SM Occupancy（流多处理器占用率）是衡量 GPU 计算资源实际利用程度的指标。它定义了在一个 SM 上同时驻留的 active warp 数量与该 SM 最大可支持 warp 数量的比值。S